{"id":"e14t1","name":"Payment Date Cleanup","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["payments_df","run_date"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Payments are collected from several regional systems. Each system writes the payment date in its own format, and some systems send invalid or empty dates. The finance team needs a clean table with a real date column.</p>\n<p>Implement <code>solve</code> so that it parses the payment dates, rejects invalid ones and returns the valid payments.</p>\n<h3>Input</h3>\n<p><code>payments_df</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>payment_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>unique, never null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>customer_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>never null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>amount</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>decimal text such as <code>\"25.50\"</code> or <code>\"40\"</code>, never null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>paid_on</td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>payment date as free text; may be null</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><code>run_date</code> is a string in the format <code>yyyy-MM-dd</code>.</p>\n<h3>Rules</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Leading and trailing spaces of <code>paid_on</code> are ignored.</li>\n<li>After trimming, <code>paid_on</code> is valid only if it matches one of these formats exactly and represents a real calendar date:</li>\n</ol>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>format</th>\n<th>example</th>\n<th>note</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>yyyy-MM-dd</code></td>\n<td><code>2024-03-05</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>d/M/yyyy</code></td>\n<td><code>5/3/2024</code>, <code>05/03/2024</code></td>\n<td>day first, then month; day and month have 1 or 2 digits</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss</code></td>\n<td><code>2024-03-05T14:30:00</code></td>\n<td>only the date part is kept</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>yyyyMMdd</code></td>\n<td><code>20240305</code></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Any other format (for example <code>03-05-2024</code> or <code>2024-03-05 14:30:00</code>), an impossible date (for example <code>2024-02-30</code>), an empty string or null is invalid.\n3. <code>payment_date</code> is the parsed date. A payment whose <code>payment_date</code> is after <code>run_date</code> is invalid.\n4. Invalid payments are excluded from the output.\n5. <code>amount</code> is converted to a double.</p>\n<p>The Spark session of the grader uses <code>spark.sql.legacy.timeParserPolicy=CORRECTED</code>: <code>to_date</code> returns null when a string does not match the given pattern.</p>\n<h3>Output</h3>\n<p>A DataFrame with exactly these columns, in this order:</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>column</th>\n<th>type</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>payment_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>customer_id</td>\n<td>string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>payment_date</td>\n<td>date</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>amount</td>\n<td>double</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Rows are sorted by <code>payment_date</code> ascending, then <code>payment_id</code> ascending.</p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p><code>run_date = \"2024-03-31\"</code></p>\n<p><code>payments_df</code></p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>payment_id</th>\n<th>customer_id</th>\n<th>amount</th>\n<th>paid_on</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>P1</td>\n<td>C1</td>\n<td>\"100.00\"</td>\n<td>\"2024-03-05\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P2</td>\n<td>C2</td>\n<td>\"25.50\"</td>\n<td>\" 5/3/2024 \"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P3</td>\n<td>C1</td>\n<td>\"40\"</td>\n<td>\"2024-03-04T23:59:59\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P4</td>\n<td>C3</td>\n<td>\"10.00\"</td>\n<td>\"20240301\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P5</td>\n<td>C2</td>\n<td>\"99.00\"</td>\n<td>\"2024-02-30\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P6</td>\n<td>C3</td>\n<td>\"15.00\"</td>\n<td>\"03-05-2024\"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P7</td>\n<td>C1</td>\n<td>\"60.00\"</td>\n<td>null</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P8</td>\n<td>C4</td>\n<td>\"70.00\"</td>\n<td>\"2024-04-02\"</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Expected output</p>\n<table class=\"mdt\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>payment_id</th>\n<th>customer_id</th>\n<th>payment_date</th>\n<th>amount</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>P4</td>\n<td>C3</td>\n<td>2024-03-01</td>\n<td>10.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P3</td>\n<td>C1</td>\n<td>2024-03-04</td>\n<td>40.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P1</td>\n<td>C1</td>\n<td>2024-03-05</td>\n<td>100.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>P2</td>\n<td>C2</td>\n<td>2024-03-05</td>\n<td>25.5</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Function signature</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">from pyspark.sql import DataFrame\n\ndef solve(payments_df: DataFrame, run_date: str) -&gt; DataFrame:\n    ...\n</code></pre>\n<h3>Constraints</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Use the PySpark DataFrame API. Do not convert to pandas, do not call <code>collect()</code> or <code>toPandas()</code> inside <code>solve</code>, and do not use Python UDFs.</li>\n<li><code>payments_df</code> has up to 10^7 rows.</li>\n<li>The returned DataFrame may be empty; its columns and types must still match the specification.</li>\n</ul><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import DataFrame, Window\nfrom pyspark.sql import functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(payments_df: DataFrame, run_date: str) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return payments_df\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":[],"minutes":22,"source":"Examen d'entraînement d'octobre n°6, question 1","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"payments_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"payment_id string, customer_id string, amount string, paid_on string","rows":[["P1","C1","100.00","2024-03-05"],["P2","C2","25.50"," 5/3/2024 "],["P3","C1","40","2024-03-04T23:59:59"],["P4","C3","10.00","20240301"],["P5","C2","99.00","2024-02-30"],["P6","C3","15.00","03-05-2024"],["P7","C1","60.00",null],["P8","C4","70.00","2024-04-02"]]}},"run_date":"2024-03-31"},"expected":{"columns":["payment_id","customer_id","payment_date","amount"],"rows":[["P4","C3","2024-03-01",10.0],["P3","C1","2024-03-04",40.0],["P1","C1","2024-03-05",100.0],["P2","C2","2024-03-05",25.5]]}}],"hidden_n":4,"hidden":"","solution":""}